00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:06,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:07,625 --> 00:00:09,025
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:36,625 --> 00:01:39,065
ADAPTED FROM THE EARLY SPRING ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:01:53,585 --> 00:01:54,745
Come in.

4
00:01:59,745 --> 00:02:02,385
So? The results are out?

5
00:02:03,705 --> 00:02:05,665
She deserves the Specialist title.

6
00:02:07,025 --> 00:02:10,584
And it turns out, about 80%
of my decisions are right,

7
00:02:10,665 --> 00:02:12,185
and 20% are wrong.

8
00:02:12,265 --> 00:02:14,585
But when it comes to people,
you made the right decisions.

9
00:02:15,185 --> 00:02:16,945
Shang Zhitao is outstanding.

10
00:02:17,025 --> 00:02:18,225
You have a good eye for talent.

11
00:02:49,905 --> 00:02:51,265
Well prepared. Who did this?

12
00:02:51,865 --> 00:02:53,705
Dony must've planted someone here
before he went to prison.

13
00:02:53,785 --> 00:02:55,265
The whistleblower was one
of his former subordinates.

14
00:02:55,345 --> 00:02:57,345
Someone who worked at Lime briefly.

15
00:02:57,425 --> 00:02:58,585
A real piece of work.

16
00:02:59,505 --> 00:03:00,865
He's like a bad penny.

17
00:03:06,385 --> 00:03:09,265
The day Flora reported him
for sexual harassment,

18
00:03:09,345 --> 00:03:11,705
you stepped in
and dealt with him yourself.

19
00:03:12,225 --> 00:03:14,185
That's when I knew something
was going on between you.

20
00:03:15,105 --> 00:03:17,665
I'd actually sensed it before then.

21
00:03:18,185 --> 00:03:21,585
I didn't say anything
because I know where your line is.

22
00:03:22,625 --> 00:03:26,065
And I trusted that she wasn't the kind
of employee who'd break the rules.

23
00:03:26,985 --> 00:03:27,825
But

24
00:03:29,265 --> 00:03:30,505
someone gave me this.

25
00:03:32,665 --> 00:03:34,185
What are you going to do with it?

26
00:03:40,265 --> 00:03:44,025
A GRAND RETREAT

27
00:03:49,905 --> 00:03:51,145
LIME ANNUAL APPRECIATION NIGHT

28
00:04:13,585 --> 00:04:14,945
Cheers, Lumi.

29
00:04:22,665 --> 00:04:24,225
Song Ying made the shortlist.
Did you know that?

30
00:04:27,145 --> 00:04:28,265
I just found out.

31
00:04:28,865 --> 00:04:33,185
Her dad is giving 80%
of next year's ad budget to Lime.

32
00:04:34,105 --> 00:04:37,145
Eighty percent? How much is that?

33
00:04:37,225 --> 00:04:39,745
Two hundred and fifty million.
Across all platforms.

34
00:04:40,465 --> 00:04:42,065
That's the power of money.

35
00:04:46,945 --> 00:04:48,065
Flora.

36
00:04:48,625 --> 00:04:50,185
-Congratulations.
-Kitty.

37
00:04:50,265 --> 00:04:51,745
You finally made Specialist this year.

38
00:04:53,265 --> 00:04:56,625
I'm telling you,
you're the most envied woman at Lime.

39
00:04:57,545 --> 00:04:58,785
Got your acceptance speech ready?

40
00:04:59,825 --> 00:05:01,105
I still need to work on it.

41
00:05:01,185 --> 00:05:02,385
Don't worry. You'll be fine.

42
00:05:02,465 --> 00:05:05,025
Flora, I just joined
the company this year.

43
00:05:05,105 --> 00:05:06,785
Please look out for me.

44
00:05:06,865 --> 00:05:08,465
-Do your best.
-Thank you.

45
00:05:08,545 --> 00:05:09,665
I'll head over first.

46
00:05:13,385 --> 00:05:15,425
Relax. It's definitely you.

47
00:05:15,505 --> 00:05:17,385
Everyone knows it.

48
00:05:17,465 --> 00:05:19,825
If she wins, people won't accept it.
It won't be her.

49
00:05:20,465 --> 00:05:22,065
If someone's going to win,

50
00:05:22,145 --> 00:05:24,385
why can't it be you?

51
00:05:24,465 --> 00:05:27,225
If it's not you,
I'll be the first to object.

52
00:05:36,825 --> 00:05:37,745
Luke.

53
00:05:44,585 --> 00:05:45,945
Thank you for your guidance and support.

54
00:05:49,385 --> 00:05:50,265
Keep up the good work.

55
00:05:57,945 --> 00:05:58,785
Let's talk later.

56
00:06:04,585 --> 00:06:07,145
Distinguished leaders, honored guests,

57
00:06:07,225 --> 00:06:10,465
ladies and gentlemen,
dear Lime family and friends,

58
00:06:10,545 --> 00:06:13,065
good evening!

59
00:06:15,265 --> 00:06:17,505
Next, it's time for our biggest award,

60
00:06:17,585 --> 00:06:20,105
the announcement
of this year's Specialist.

61
00:06:20,185 --> 00:06:23,665
Lime is the leading advertising agency
in the industry.

62
00:06:23,745 --> 00:06:25,745
The Specialist we choose each year

63
00:06:25,825 --> 00:06:31,505
must have made outstanding contributions
and achieved remarkable results.

64
00:06:31,585 --> 00:06:34,665
They'll help lead the advertising industry
to new heights

65
00:06:34,745 --> 00:06:37,065
and serve as an example to us all.

66
00:06:37,145 --> 00:06:41,305
This year's finalists
are the head of the Northwest project,

67
00:06:41,385 --> 00:06:45,345
who has served the company
faithfully for six years, Flora.

68
00:06:47,025 --> 00:06:48,505
-Thank you.
-Shang Zhitao.

69
00:06:48,585 --> 00:06:50,065
I love you.

70
00:06:50,145 --> 00:06:51,385
THE LEGEND IS HERE!

71
00:06:53,145 --> 00:06:55,265
And the second finalist,
who was selected by exception,

72
00:06:55,345 --> 00:06:56,185
a rising star in the industry

73
00:06:56,265 --> 00:07:01,625
who secured the company's
biggest account of the year, Yilia.

74
00:07:07,105 --> 00:07:09,545
Who will take home the title?

75
00:07:09,625 --> 00:07:13,865
Now, please welcome Luke,
the General Manager of Lime Advertising,

76
00:07:13,945 --> 00:07:18,865
to announce this year's Specialist.

77
00:07:18,945 --> 00:07:20,145
A big round of applause.

78
00:07:51,865 --> 00:07:52,945
This year's

79
00:07:54,905 --> 00:07:56,745
Lime Specialist is…

80
00:08:01,985 --> 00:08:03,465
Yilia, Song Ying.

81
00:08:49,185 --> 00:08:51,185
SONG YING, LIME SPECIALIST

82
00:08:51,265 --> 00:08:52,105
Thank you.

83
00:08:55,025 --> 00:08:59,385
Alright. Yilia, how do you feel
about winning this honor?

84
00:08:59,465 --> 00:09:01,185
Thank you to the company
for this recognition.

85
00:09:01,945 --> 00:09:05,025
I'd like to share this honor with Flora.

86
00:09:11,225 --> 00:09:12,945
I… Thank you.

87
00:09:23,905 --> 00:09:25,905
It belongs to you.

88
00:09:25,985 --> 00:09:27,145
You've done an incredible job.

89
00:09:27,825 --> 00:09:30,665
When I was your age,
I wasn't anywhere near as good.

90
00:09:31,625 --> 00:09:33,425
I was completely ordinary.

91
00:09:34,305 --> 00:09:37,185
It was an honor to compete with you.

92
00:09:37,265 --> 00:09:38,385
Congratulations.

93
00:09:38,465 --> 00:09:40,785
Alright. Thank you both
for your wonderful speeches.

94
00:09:40,865 --> 00:09:43,545
Now, let the banquet begin.

95
00:10:44,105 --> 00:10:45,425
Please excuse me.

96
00:11:27,625 --> 00:11:28,665
Are you okay?

97
00:11:31,665 --> 00:11:34,625
Sun Yu and I are catching
a midnight movie later.

98
00:11:38,065 --> 00:11:39,185
Is Sun Yuanzhu not coming?

99
00:11:48,945 --> 00:11:51,145
You knew today's result, didn't you?

100
00:11:55,905 --> 00:11:57,705
Why didn't you tell me beforehand?

101
00:11:59,265 --> 00:12:00,785
Would that have changed the outcome?

102
00:12:02,985 --> 00:12:03,945
Of course not.

103
00:12:07,425 --> 00:12:10,665
But Lumi knew Song Ying
was competing against me.

104
00:12:10,745 --> 00:12:12,625
She told me in advance.

105
00:12:12,705 --> 00:12:14,905
You've been my superior for years.

106
00:12:14,985 --> 00:12:17,745
You knew how much
I'd put into this project.

107
00:12:18,265 --> 00:12:19,185
And you just sat there,

108
00:12:19,265 --> 00:12:22,385
watching me wait in anticipation
below the stage like a clown.

109
00:12:23,865 --> 00:12:27,185
If it wasn't Song Ying,
it would've been someone else.

110
00:12:29,225 --> 00:12:31,625
Everyone can see how hard you've worked,
what you've achieved,

111
00:12:31,705 --> 00:12:32,785
and what you're capable of.

112
00:12:33,425 --> 00:12:34,745
If you know you've done well,

113
00:12:35,585 --> 00:12:37,105
don't let other people's
opinions get to you.

114
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:40,505
Then tell me.

115
00:12:44,145 --> 00:12:46,225
Would you have scored me fairly?

116
00:12:48,825 --> 00:12:49,865
What do you mean?

117
00:12:49,945 --> 00:12:51,225
Could you, Luan Nian,

118
00:12:53,185 --> 00:12:58,145
ignore that 250 million
and judge me fairly and objectively?

119
00:12:58,225 --> 00:12:59,425
Could you?

120
00:13:10,705 --> 00:13:13,585
Shang Zhitao,
this was another competition.

121
00:13:14,505 --> 00:13:16,385
Is it really that hard
to focus on doing your best?

122
00:13:17,185 --> 00:13:18,585
One result doesn't define you.

123
00:13:19,185 --> 00:13:22,705
As long as you keep doing well,
next time will be yours.

124
00:13:27,825 --> 00:13:28,985
This is the workplace, I know.

125
00:13:30,385 --> 00:13:32,505
Things are never completely fair.

126
00:13:32,585 --> 00:13:35,065
Relationships, connections, money.

127
00:13:35,145 --> 00:13:36,585
They can all come before ability.

128
00:13:36,665 --> 00:13:38,105
But I always thought this was different.

129
00:13:38,185 --> 00:13:40,265
Because it was Lime.

130
00:13:40,345 --> 00:13:43,665
It's the Lime that made an exception
to hire me and helped me grow so quickly.

131
00:13:43,745 --> 00:13:45,505
It was fair and objective.

132
00:13:45,585 --> 00:13:47,745
Anything was possible here.

133
00:13:48,705 --> 00:13:51,105
That's why I never thought I'd lose.

134
00:13:51,905 --> 00:13:53,545
And I don't want to be
the last one to know

135
00:13:53,625 --> 00:13:55,385
that the outcome was already decided.

136
00:13:56,585 --> 00:13:58,825
Shang Zhitao, I never thought you were
someone who couldn't handle losing.

137
00:14:00,265 --> 00:14:01,945
There are winners and losers
in the workplace.

138
00:14:02,025 --> 00:14:04,145
Adults should know
how to accept the result.

139
00:14:05,345 --> 00:14:08,065
You're only this upset because
you think I didn't treat you differently.

140
00:14:08,145 --> 00:14:09,145
Am I right?

141
00:14:09,945 --> 00:14:11,145
Let me tell you this.

142
00:14:11,225 --> 00:14:13,385
I keep work and personal life
completely separate.

143
00:14:13,465 --> 00:14:14,985
I suggest you do the same.

144
00:14:15,785 --> 00:14:16,945
Otherwise, you're only making things
harder for yourself.

145
00:14:18,625 --> 00:14:19,825
I'm not like you.

146
00:14:22,225 --> 00:14:25,625
You can afford to lose with grace.

147
00:14:25,705 --> 00:14:27,185
I can't.

148
00:14:27,265 --> 00:14:31,385
From the first day I joined Lime,
all I've wanted was to survive here.

149
00:14:32,385 --> 00:14:35,105
Every single step I've taken
is like walking on thin ice.

150
00:14:35,185 --> 00:14:36,345
Do you understand?

151
00:14:43,305 --> 00:14:44,705
Luan Nian,

152
00:14:46,265 --> 00:14:47,425
of course you don't understand.

153
00:14:48,065 --> 00:14:49,945
If you did,
you wouldn't have asked me that.

154
00:14:50,025 --> 00:14:52,105
You wouldn't be talking to me like this.

155
00:14:53,905 --> 00:14:55,545
You've always looked down on me.

156
00:14:55,625 --> 00:14:56,665
You never believed I was good enough.

157
00:14:56,745 --> 00:14:57,905
You never thought I had what it takes.

158
00:14:57,985 --> 00:15:01,265
You've never respected me
or treated me as your equal.

159
00:15:01,345 --> 00:15:04,385
Why did I spend six years
with someone like you?

160
00:15:10,345 --> 00:15:11,585
What kind of person do you think I am?

161
00:15:16,865 --> 00:15:20,785
Arrogant. Conceited. Selfish.

162
00:15:24,305 --> 00:15:25,825
Is that really how you see me?

163
00:15:27,705 --> 00:15:29,585
Why do you always question me?

164
00:15:29,665 --> 00:15:31,425
Why am I always the one being doubted?

165
00:15:31,505 --> 00:15:34,465
Why are you always so condescending?

166
00:15:34,545 --> 00:15:35,945
Luan Nian.

167
00:15:37,545 --> 00:15:40,585
Is it really that hard
to talk to me properly?

168
00:15:44,985 --> 00:15:46,745
Shang Zhitao, you should calm down now.

169
00:15:49,105 --> 00:15:50,745
Why should I?

170
00:15:50,825 --> 00:15:52,465
Why do I have to calm down?

171
00:15:52,545 --> 00:15:55,305
I've struggled in this city for six years,

172
00:15:55,385 --> 00:15:57,105
and in the end, I've got nothing.

173
00:15:57,185 --> 00:15:58,825
I lost my best friend.

174
00:15:58,905 --> 00:16:01,425
I lost the competition I should've won.

175
00:16:01,505 --> 00:16:03,105
And now you're telling me to calm down.

176
00:16:03,185 --> 00:16:04,425
What gives you the right?

177
00:16:07,785 --> 00:16:09,505
My patience is wearing thin.

178
00:16:10,385 --> 00:16:11,745
Stop pushing me.

179
00:16:56,745 --> 00:16:58,985
I want to end this.

180
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:25,625
End what?

181
00:17:27,545 --> 00:17:28,785
What are you ending?

182
00:17:38,785 --> 00:17:40,625
I'm ending…

183
00:17:44,665 --> 00:17:45,665
this filthy,

184
00:17:47,185 --> 00:17:48,265
ugly,

185
00:17:50,745 --> 00:17:52,385
disgusting relationship between us.

186
00:17:59,265 --> 00:18:01,665
You think our relationship was filthy?

187
00:18:02,185 --> 00:18:05,465
Ugly? Disgusting?

188
00:18:07,905 --> 00:18:10,545
It was never a normal relationship.

189
00:18:11,625 --> 00:18:13,865
We never trusted each other.

190
00:18:16,625 --> 00:18:18,665
We never loved each other.

191
00:18:25,545 --> 00:18:28,505
So you were only with me
to get ahead in your career?

192
00:18:29,385 --> 00:18:33,265
And now that you lost,
you think I've outlived my usefulness?

193
00:18:34,425 --> 00:18:36,425
The main reason I lost

194
00:18:36,505 --> 00:18:40,065
was spending six years
with someone like you.

195
00:18:40,145 --> 00:18:43,505
Someone who couldn't judge me fairly.

196
00:18:43,585 --> 00:18:44,425
Exactly.

197
00:18:46,265 --> 00:18:47,585
You said it yourself.

198
00:18:47,665 --> 00:18:49,025
We were only together for six years.

199
00:18:49,545 --> 00:18:50,985
There weren't any real feelings.

200
00:18:51,745 --> 00:18:55,545
If it wasn't you,
it could've been someone else.

201
00:19:26,905 --> 00:19:28,025
Let's end it here.

202
00:20:04,745 --> 00:20:07,825
I can't accept adding Yilia
to this year's Specialist selection.

203
00:20:08,825 --> 00:20:10,545
She hasn't been here long enough.

204
00:20:10,625 --> 00:20:12,185
She doesn't meet
the company's requirements.

205
00:20:12,265 --> 00:20:14,305
You know this.

206
00:20:14,385 --> 00:20:16,905
It was a special exception by the board.

207
00:20:17,585 --> 00:20:18,625
I don't agree.

208
00:20:18,705 --> 00:20:21,385
Luke, it's only an extra candidate.

209
00:20:25,265 --> 00:20:26,825
You and I both know

210
00:20:27,425 --> 00:20:30,225
Flora deserves
this year's Specialist title.

211
00:20:30,985 --> 00:20:32,945
She spent over a year
working in the Northwest for this project.

212
00:20:34,665 --> 00:20:40,065
And you also know Yilia brought Lime
250 million in ad spending.

213
00:20:40,145 --> 00:20:41,625
That's enough to change the rules.

214
00:20:41,705 --> 00:20:44,785
I admit Yilia is capable.
She's delivered results.

215
00:20:44,865 --> 00:20:45,825
You can promote her,

216
00:20:45,905 --> 00:20:48,425
give her a raise,
or a huge bonus if you want,

217
00:20:48,505 --> 00:20:51,265
but the Specialist title recognizes
ability, seniority, and experience.

218
00:20:51,345 --> 00:20:53,745
I won't accept the company
changing the rules on a whim.

219
00:21:02,265 --> 00:21:03,265
What are you going to do?

220
00:21:03,905 --> 00:21:06,265
I pulled some records as requested.

221
00:21:06,985 --> 00:21:09,985
The first person Flora informed
about weekend overtime was you.

222
00:21:10,505 --> 00:21:12,985
The first person
she traveled with was you.

223
00:21:13,065 --> 00:21:15,185
The security footage was reviewed too.

224
00:21:15,265 --> 00:21:18,345
Every Friday night, you two always left
the office one after the other.

225
00:21:18,425 --> 00:21:22,465
You know those facts can't be changed.

226
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:25,665
Fine.

227
00:21:26,265 --> 00:21:28,185
I'll leave. I'll resign.

228
00:21:28,265 --> 00:21:30,185
But you know perfectly well,

229
00:21:30,265 --> 00:21:32,145
if you leave,
she won't be able to stay either.

230
00:21:41,545 --> 00:21:43,105
I'm due to report to the US.

231
00:21:43,745 --> 00:21:45,665
There's an opening
for President over there.

232
00:21:45,745 --> 00:21:46,705
I turned it down before.

233
00:21:48,185 --> 00:21:51,225
Now I can apply for the transfer.

234
00:21:51,305 --> 00:21:52,785
On one condition.

235
00:21:52,865 --> 00:21:54,825
Flora stays at Lime.

236
00:22:00,185 --> 00:22:02,265
This job means everything to her.

237
00:22:03,705 --> 00:22:05,425
I know.

238
00:22:06,305 --> 00:22:09,945
I've watched her fight
her way up over the past six years.

239
00:22:10,025 --> 00:22:11,505
I want her to stay too.

240
00:22:13,185 --> 00:22:18,385
But this year's Specialist title
must go to Yilia.

241
00:22:20,105 --> 00:22:21,225
Give it to Yilia then.

242
00:22:21,745 --> 00:22:25,665
Next year, create
another Specialist position for Flora.

243
00:22:27,385 --> 00:22:30,025
Don't worry.
I'll do everything I can for her.

244
00:22:34,585 --> 00:22:37,825
Never thought you'd actually fall in love.

245
00:22:40,945 --> 00:22:42,305
I have one more request.

246
00:22:42,945 --> 00:22:44,385
Keep all this from Flora.

247
00:22:45,985 --> 00:22:46,985
Why?

248
00:22:47,665 --> 00:22:50,025
Wouldn't it be better
if she knew what you've done for her?

249
00:22:52,745 --> 00:22:54,105
She's too proud.

250
00:22:54,785 --> 00:22:59,385
If she finds out,
she'll either leave Lime or leave me.

251
00:23:01,665 --> 00:23:04,065
Alright. You have my word.

252
00:23:08,985 --> 00:23:09,825
Thank you.

253
00:23:14,305 --> 00:23:15,825
I'm ending

254
00:23:17,625 --> 00:23:21,465
this filthy, ugly,
disgusting relationship between us.

255
00:23:37,865 --> 00:23:40,345
You're only this upset because
you think I didn't treat you specially.

256
00:23:40,425 --> 00:23:41,305
Am I right?

257
00:23:41,385 --> 00:23:44,025
I keep work and personal life
completely separate.

258
00:23:44,105 --> 00:23:45,665
I suggest you do the same.

259
00:23:46,345 --> 00:23:47,785
Otherwise, you're only
making things harder for yourself.

260
00:23:48,625 --> 00:23:50,345
We were only together for six years.

261
00:23:50,425 --> 00:23:52,185
If it wasn't you,

262
00:23:52,985 --> 00:23:54,105
it could've been someone else.

263
00:24:34,145 --> 00:24:34,985
Shang Zhitao,

264
00:24:36,305 --> 00:24:37,545
don't be impulsive.

265
00:24:38,505 --> 00:24:40,745
I'm not. I'm taking Luke with me.

266
00:24:43,505 --> 00:24:44,865
You're an adult.

267
00:24:48,305 --> 00:24:49,385
If you say it's over,

268
00:24:50,425 --> 00:24:51,705
then don't ever start it again.

269
00:25:01,985 --> 00:25:03,225
I never will.

270
00:25:13,785 --> 00:25:15,345
Let's go, Luke.

271
00:25:16,665 --> 00:25:17,585
Come on, Luke.

272
00:25:25,985 --> 00:25:27,105
Luke.

273
00:25:37,985 --> 00:25:39,505
Listen.

274
00:25:39,585 --> 00:25:41,545
You can only choose one.

275
00:25:41,625 --> 00:25:42,905
If you stay,

276
00:25:42,985 --> 00:25:44,705
you'll never see me again.

277
00:25:45,505 --> 00:25:46,385
Luke.

278
00:25:50,425 --> 00:25:51,305
We're leaving.

279
00:25:57,585 --> 00:25:58,465
Let's go, Luke.

280
00:25:59,145 --> 00:26:01,345
Come on. Let's go, Luke.

281
00:26:11,145 --> 00:26:12,385
You're staying, aren't you?

282
00:26:16,065 --> 00:26:16,905
Fine.

283
00:26:21,985 --> 00:26:24,145
You stay. I'll go.

284
00:27:31,945 --> 00:27:34,545
You ungrateful Luke,
you chose the rich over the poor.

285
00:27:34,625 --> 00:27:36,105
Even you betrayed me.

286
00:28:08,385 --> 00:28:10,065
Luke.

287
00:28:13,865 --> 00:28:15,865
Thank you, Luke.

288
00:29:16,305 --> 00:29:18,185
We'll start a new life together.

289
00:30:06,465 --> 00:30:07,385
Here's some warm water.

290
00:30:16,465 --> 00:30:17,305
Sun Yu.

291
00:30:23,585 --> 00:30:25,465
I didn't get promoted.

292
00:30:27,945 --> 00:30:29,425
I prepared for so long.

293
00:30:30,585 --> 00:30:32,225
I really thought I'd win.

294
00:30:34,985 --> 00:30:36,145
But I lost.

295
00:30:37,465 --> 00:30:38,505
I…

296
00:30:43,145 --> 00:30:43,985
I…

297
00:30:50,785 --> 00:30:52,745
I let Zhu down

298
00:30:54,305 --> 00:30:57,625
after everything he did for me.

299
00:31:06,825 --> 00:31:10,585
Tao, don't scare me.

300
00:31:10,665 --> 00:31:12,705
Promise me you won't do anything silly.

301
00:31:14,105 --> 00:31:15,585
You know that.

302
00:31:17,585 --> 00:31:19,385
I can't lose another friend. You hear me?

303
00:31:22,585 --> 00:31:24,465
Don't cry. I can't handle it when you cry.

304
00:31:24,545 --> 00:31:25,745
Please don't cry.

305
00:31:33,145 --> 00:31:34,625
Please don't cry.

306
00:31:42,305 --> 00:31:43,425
Take this.

307
00:31:55,305 --> 00:31:57,065
My company's doing great now.

308
00:31:57,825 --> 00:32:00,745
I'd sincerely like to invite you
to be our Vice President.

309
00:32:00,825 --> 00:32:03,705
Once we secure Series C funding,
we'll expand into the south.

310
00:32:04,345 --> 00:32:08,425
With your ability, you could be
an executive at any company.

311
00:32:09,425 --> 00:32:10,665
Can I still steal you away?

312
00:32:13,105 --> 00:32:17,665
I'll have HR talk to you
about the salary, alright?

313
00:32:19,065 --> 00:32:19,905
No more crying.

314
00:32:23,385 --> 00:32:24,345
Don't worry.

315
00:32:25,425 --> 00:32:26,425
I'm okay.

316
00:32:27,105 --> 00:32:28,105
I just

317
00:32:29,985 --> 00:32:31,305
broke up.

318
00:32:33,505 --> 00:32:35,665
I haven't gotten over it yet. I…

319
00:32:39,825 --> 00:32:40,705
It…

320
00:32:43,025 --> 00:32:43,985
It hurts.

321
00:33:48,465 --> 00:33:49,305
MOM

322
00:33:49,385 --> 00:33:51,825
Tao, when are you taking leave?

323
00:33:51,905 --> 00:33:53,785
Your dad told me not to tell you,

324
00:33:53,865 --> 00:33:55,385
but he fell downstairs a few days ago.

325
00:33:55,465 --> 00:33:56,745
He broke a bone.

326
00:33:56,825 --> 00:33:58,945
He keeps saying he wants to see you.

327
00:33:59,025 --> 00:34:01,825
Can you take a few days off

328
00:34:01,905 --> 00:34:03,945
and come home early?

329
00:34:04,025 --> 00:34:05,185
If you're too busy, then forget it.

330
00:34:27,744 --> 00:34:29,185
Got it, Luke.

331
00:34:58,345 --> 00:35:00,985
-Where are you going?
-To hand in my resignation.

332
00:35:28,465 --> 00:35:29,305
Luke.

333
00:35:34,065 --> 00:35:35,905
That's fast.

334
00:35:35,985 --> 00:35:37,425
Are you leaving for the US next week?

335
00:35:37,505 --> 00:35:39,785
The position has been vacant.

336
00:35:39,865 --> 00:35:41,825
They want me there early to take over.

337
00:35:42,425 --> 00:35:43,585
See you.

338
00:36:40,065 --> 00:36:42,225
RESIGNATION FORM, SHANG ZHITAO

339
00:36:46,905 --> 00:36:51,185
Flora, there'll be another
Specialist selection next year.

340
00:36:53,585 --> 00:36:55,905
I'll do my best to help you get it.

341
00:36:59,345 --> 00:37:00,825
Thank you, Tracy,

342
00:37:00,905 --> 00:37:03,145
but I'm not leaving because of that.

343
00:37:05,825 --> 00:37:06,985
You don't need to thank me.

344
00:37:07,545 --> 00:37:08,905
If anyone deserves thanks,

345
00:37:08,985 --> 00:37:10,505
it's you,

346
00:37:10,585 --> 00:37:14,265
for all your hard work
and perseverance over the years.

347
00:37:17,385 --> 00:37:18,545
I still want to thank you.

348
00:37:19,585 --> 00:37:22,985
Thank you for helping me
and encouraging me.

349
00:37:26,345 --> 00:37:28,625
I've already bought my ticket home.

350
00:37:29,305 --> 00:37:30,705
Please sign it for me.

351
00:37:32,905 --> 00:37:33,865
Flora.

352
00:37:34,945 --> 00:37:38,905
I hired you myself.

353
00:37:38,985 --> 00:37:43,825
I've watched you work hard
and earn everything you have today.

354
00:37:44,425 --> 00:37:45,625
I'm proud of you.

355
00:37:45,705 --> 00:37:47,905
So hearing you resign,

356
00:37:47,985 --> 00:37:50,825
I really hate to see you go.

357
00:37:52,185 --> 00:37:53,985
I hope you'll think it over.

358
00:37:55,225 --> 00:37:57,265
Not just for yourself,
but also for your career,

359
00:37:59,665 --> 00:38:00,905
and Luke too.

360
00:38:08,265 --> 00:38:13,545
I… I heard from Lumi
that Luke's going to the US.

361
00:38:14,985 --> 00:38:18,865
At my level, I don't think my resignation
needs his approval.

362
00:38:20,785 --> 00:38:21,785
Tracy.

363
00:38:23,665 --> 00:38:25,385
Just help me one last time.

364
00:38:26,625 --> 00:38:27,905
Please sign it.

365
00:38:28,745 --> 00:38:30,465
Something happened at home.

366
00:38:30,545 --> 00:38:31,945
I have to go back.

367
00:38:40,905 --> 00:38:42,145
Alright.

368
00:39:01,665 --> 00:39:02,625
Thank you, Tracy.

369
00:39:18,425 --> 00:39:20,905
Your first rotation
is with Business Division One.

370
00:39:22,825 --> 00:39:23,745
You can sit here.

371
00:39:24,425 --> 00:39:26,905
Lumi, I'm Shang Zhitao.

372
00:39:26,985 --> 00:39:28,065
My English name is Flora.

373
00:39:29,225 --> 00:39:30,185
Since Lime hired me,

374
00:39:30,265 --> 00:39:33,265
I believe I have something of value.

375
00:39:33,345 --> 00:39:36,505
Being able to join the world's top
advertising agency and broaden my horizons

376
00:39:36,585 --> 00:39:38,665
is both an honor and a stroke of luck.

377
00:39:38,745 --> 00:39:40,585
I'll work hard and earn my place here.

378
00:40:51,305 --> 00:40:53,545
Goodbye, Lime.

379
00:41:09,705 --> 00:41:10,945
Have some water.

380
00:41:11,025 --> 00:41:12,105
Thanks.

381
00:41:14,785 --> 00:41:17,785
Do either of you
have Zhu's family's contact?

382
00:41:19,545 --> 00:41:20,425
Why?

383
00:41:21,305 --> 00:41:22,905
I still owe him money.

384
00:41:25,545 --> 00:41:27,265
I might as well tell you now.

385
00:41:27,945 --> 00:41:30,065
The money my ex-wife and I used
to buy the apartment

386
00:41:30,745 --> 00:41:32,065
was borrowed from Zhu.

387
00:41:33,465 --> 00:41:35,225
He told me not to tell you.

388
00:41:35,305 --> 00:41:37,025
He said he wanted to give you two a home.

389
00:41:39,985 --> 00:41:43,225
But before you could enjoy it for long,
the family fell apart.

390
00:41:51,305 --> 00:41:52,505
One of you is heading south,

391
00:41:52,585 --> 00:41:54,185
and the other is going back home.

392
00:41:54,265 --> 00:41:55,905
So I thought

393
00:41:56,425 --> 00:41:58,865
while the housing market was still good,
I'd sell the apartment.

394
00:41:59,665 --> 00:42:03,385
He's gone now,
but I still owe it to his family.

395
00:42:04,185 --> 00:42:05,985
If you sell the apartment,
where will you live?

396
00:42:06,785 --> 00:42:08,505
Me? I got promoted.

397
00:42:08,585 --> 00:42:11,505
The company's giving me a dorm,
so I'll save on rent.

398
00:42:13,305 --> 00:42:14,345
From now on,

399
00:42:14,425 --> 00:42:17,305
call me Deputy Product Manager
of the Marketing Department.

400
00:42:20,185 --> 00:42:21,465
You got promoted.
Dinner's on you then, Lei?

401
00:42:22,065 --> 00:42:22,945
Of course.

402
00:42:23,025 --> 00:42:24,985
Let's go somewhere expensive then.
Same as always.

403
00:42:25,705 --> 00:42:26,825
Works for me.

404
00:42:27,785 --> 00:42:30,785
When I get back home,
I'm changing my phone number.

405
00:42:32,185 --> 00:42:37,985
The day I call you again
will be the day I have truly started over.

406
00:42:42,185 --> 00:42:43,825
We'll all be doing better.

407
00:42:49,985 --> 00:42:51,225
Before you go,

408
00:42:52,065 --> 00:42:52,945
let's take one last photo.

409
00:42:53,465 --> 00:42:54,825
Sure. Let's take one.

410
00:42:56,545 --> 00:42:57,505
Let's…

411
00:42:57,585 --> 00:42:59,345
-Let's take one with this.
-Okay.

412
00:43:11,585 --> 00:43:12,665
I'll go get the car.

413
00:43:17,545 --> 00:43:19,465
-Thank you, Lei.
-Don't mention it.

414
00:43:20,865 --> 00:43:22,105
Open the trunk.

415
00:43:34,825 --> 00:43:38,265
Tonight, I'm cooking for you guys.

416
00:43:38,345 --> 00:43:40,625
I just learned a new dish.
Lightning Five Whips!

417
00:43:40,705 --> 00:43:42,225
-How is that?
-That's the name of a dish?

418
00:43:45,545 --> 00:43:47,865
Tao. Tao.

419
00:43:49,145 --> 00:43:50,065
We're leaving. Get in.

420
00:43:50,785 --> 00:43:51,625
Here.

421
00:43:53,825 --> 00:43:54,665
Hop in.

422
00:43:55,385 --> 00:43:58,385
TIANTONG DONGYUAN

423
00:43:58,465 --> 00:44:00,625
TIANTONGYUAN GYMNASIUM

424
00:44:00,705 --> 00:44:01,985
TIANTONG RENHE TCM HOSPITAL

425
00:44:06,385 --> 00:44:07,465
Tao,

426
00:44:08,625 --> 00:44:10,225
take good care of yourself
when you get home.

427
00:44:12,305 --> 00:44:13,865
Call me, okay?

428
00:44:15,105 --> 00:44:17,385
Yeah. Take care, Tao.

429
00:44:17,465 --> 00:44:18,625
If anyone gives you a hard time,

430
00:44:18,705 --> 00:44:19,865
call me right away.

431
00:44:19,945 --> 00:44:21,545
I'll fly over and beat them up.

432
00:44:24,145 --> 00:44:24,985
Alright.

433
00:44:26,145 --> 00:44:27,745
I have your word on that.

434
00:44:27,825 --> 00:44:28,665
You do.

435
00:45:05,665 --> 00:45:06,905
LUMI

436
00:45:06,985 --> 00:45:09,465
I'm going to miss you, Lumi.

437
00:45:16,385 --> 00:45:18,785
SHANG ZHITAO: I'M GOING TO MISS YOU, LUMI

438
00:45:21,785 --> 00:45:23,465
I hate goodbye.

439
00:45:24,065 --> 00:45:27,385
Shang Zhitao, you heartless little thing.

440
00:45:39,945 --> 00:45:43,505
Shang Zhitao, you'd better live well.

441
00:45:50,545 --> 00:45:53,105
Could I have another osmanthus milk?

442
00:46:03,825 --> 00:46:08,065
LUAN NIAN

443
00:46:18,905 --> 00:46:22,585
LUAN NIAN

444
00:46:24,585 --> 00:46:26,745
Thank you for these past six years.

445
00:46:28,665 --> 00:46:30,025
All the best.

446
00:46:38,785 --> 00:46:41,945
LUAN NIAN

447
00:46:42,025 --> 00:46:44,425
BLOCK THIS CALLER

448
00:46:56,505 --> 00:46:57,945
This isn't running away.

449
00:47:01,025 --> 00:47:04,265
It is a grand retreat.

450
00:47:05,865 --> 00:47:07,985
Because I want to give myself
another possibility.

451
00:47:13,585 --> 00:47:15,345
BEIJING TO HARBIN

452
00:47:17,425 --> 00:47:18,345
Goodbye,

453
00:47:19,625 --> 00:47:20,465
Beijing.

454
00:47:47,985 --> 00:47:49,465
Shang Zhitao.

455
00:47:50,705 --> 00:47:53,465
Are these all limited editions?

456
00:47:54,425 --> 00:47:56,065
Not bad.

457
00:47:56,145 --> 00:47:58,065
Lime has treated you well
these past years.

458
00:48:00,825 --> 00:48:04,665
The company has that year-end flea market.

459
00:48:04,745 --> 00:48:06,945
I'm leaving, so I won't make it.

460
00:48:07,025 --> 00:48:08,705
Help me sell these.

461
00:48:08,785 --> 00:48:10,185
Half price to our colleagues.

462
00:48:11,105 --> 00:48:12,945
Then we'll split the money.

463
00:48:13,025 --> 00:48:14,265
Just get rid of them quickly.

464
00:48:15,145 --> 00:48:16,505
You didn't buy these yourself, did you?

465
00:48:18,225 --> 00:48:21,105
They were gifts from my boyfriend.

466
00:48:21,185 --> 00:48:22,505
Luke bought them for you?

467
00:48:24,705 --> 00:48:27,425
You didn't really think I couldn't tell,
did you?

468
00:48:27,505 --> 00:48:29,985
You're leaving now.
I don't have to pretend anymore.

469
00:48:34,585 --> 00:48:36,265
It's all over.

470
00:48:37,985 --> 00:48:39,345
I'm leaving

471
00:48:41,625 --> 00:48:43,025
Beijing.

472
00:48:46,105 --> 00:48:47,145
Why?

473
00:48:49,905 --> 00:48:51,665
My dad hurt his leg.

474
00:48:53,025 --> 00:48:54,065
People always say,

475
00:48:54,145 --> 00:48:56,145
"When your parents are alive,
don't live too far away."

476
00:48:57,025 --> 00:48:59,065
I've been chasing this dream for years.

477
00:49:00,745 --> 00:49:03,265
I'm tired. I want to go home.

478
00:49:03,865 --> 00:49:06,745
I've already arranged for Luke
to be taken to Harbin.

479
00:49:06,825 --> 00:49:10,065
From now on,
he's officially a Northeastern pup.

480
00:49:12,505 --> 00:49:16,145
You're really giving up
everything you've built in Beijing?

481
00:49:17,225 --> 00:49:18,745
Do you have no regrets?

482
00:49:31,985 --> 00:49:35,585
Thinking about it now, career growth,

483
00:49:36,505 --> 00:49:39,705
double the salary,
none of it really matters.

484
00:49:42,065 --> 00:49:44,065
I don't need to prove myself
anymore to anyone.

485
00:49:44,825 --> 00:49:48,825
I think being with my parents
is what really matters.

486
00:49:52,785 --> 00:49:54,585
You've had an epiphany.

487
00:50:00,505 --> 00:50:01,865
Screw this job.

488
00:50:02,465 --> 00:50:04,785
I wish you all the best. Shang Zhitao.

489
00:50:07,145 --> 00:50:09,385
If you ever need anything,
you can always come to me.

490
00:50:09,465 --> 00:50:10,705
Okay?

491
00:50:11,865 --> 00:50:13,345
If anyone bullies you, I'll beat them up.

492
00:50:17,945 --> 00:50:19,905
Enough with the sad stuff.
What should we eat today?

493
00:50:21,225 --> 00:50:23,265
My treat. Deal?

494
00:50:23,345 --> 00:50:25,145
We'll meet again. I promise.

